      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/mystery-man.svg",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "gm": "",
          "value": "When the specter damages a living creature with its vile touch Strike, the specter gains 5 temporary Hit Points and the target creature must attempt a DC 25 Will save to avoid becoming corrupted. <br><b>Critical Success</b> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to spectral corruption for 1 minute. <br><b>Success</b> The creature is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.e1XGnhKNSQIm5IXg]{Stupefied} 2 for 1 hour. <br><b>Failure</b> The creature succumbs to the corruption and becomes a spectral thrall. The creature is controlled by the specter, obeying the specter's telepathic or spoken orders, though a spectral thrall does not obey obviously self-destructive orders. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns; on a success, it is no longer controlled by the specter but becomes stupefied 2 for 1 hour. <br><b>Critical Failure</b> As failure, but the creature remains a thrall to the specter until the curse is removed or until the specter succumbs to pain starvation; it can't attempt new Will saves to recover on its own.",
          "chat": "",
          "unidentified": ""
        },
